WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.287
Formatting changes how a value is displayed without
changing the underlying value stored in Python

00:00:06.211 --> 00:00:11.855
For financial results we often want thousands
separators and a fixed number of decimal places

00:00:12.789 --> 00:00:18.753
For rates we often want percentage formatting In the
example revenue

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:23.940
is displayed as money with commas and two decimal
places Growth is stored as a

00:00:23.953 --> 00:00:30.063
decimal fraction but displayed as a percentage That
distinction is important

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.697
A growth value of zero point one five represents
fifteen percent The stored value

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:42.039
and the displayed value are related but they are not
written the same way Consistent

00:00:42.066 --> 00:00:46.460
formatting makes analytical reports easier to scan
and reduces ambiguity
